This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the GPIO pins and the SPI interface. It sets up the GPIO pins, SPI interface, and motor shutdown pin, then enters a loop where it samples the current every second, converts the ADC reading to amperes, logs the current to a file, and checks for over-current conditions. If the current exceeds 10.0 A, it drives the motor shutdown pin low, logs the over-current event, waits one second, then drives the motor shutdown pin high again. The code also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to clean up resources and exit cleanly.

