This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO and SPI interfaces on the Raspberry Pi. It continuously reads the ADC value from the MCP3008 chip and checks if it exceeds the defined threshold. If it does, it logs the event and turns on the LED for 500ms. The program also installs a SIGINT handler to cleanly release resources when the user presses Ctrl+C.

