        usleep(POLL_INTERVAL * 1000);
    }

    // Release all allocated resources
    gpioTerminate();
    return 0;
}
```

This code uses the `pigpio` library to control the GPIO pins and generate PWM signals for the servos. It also uses the `signal` function to set up a signal handler for SIGINT, which releases all allocated resources when the program is interrupted. The main loop polls the button states every 50ms and adjusts the corresponding axis accordingly. The servo positions are clamped to the range 25-125.

