This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a signal handler for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` to clean up resources when the program is interrupted. The program continuously monitors GPIO17 for a falling edge, waits for a 50ms debounce period, and captures an image when a valid motion event is detected. The captured image is saved to the `/home/pi/images` directory with a timestamped filename. Any errors during image capture are logged to the `/home/pi/motion_capture.log` file.

