This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins and the `i2c-dev` library to interact with the I2C bus. It sets up the VL53L1X sensor for continuous ranging mode and reads distance measurements every 500ms. If the measured distance falls below the threshold, it activates the buzzer. The code also handles I2C errors by logging the error and skipping the current iteration. The signal handler for SIGINT is set up to ensure clean resource release on exit.

