This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the I2C bus and GPIO. It initializes the library, opens the I2C bus, sets up the I2C bus, and opens a file for writing. It then enters a loop where it waits for 5 seconds, waits for 10 ms, reads the temperature and pressure from the sensor, converts the data, gets the current time, and writes the data to the file and stdout. If an I2C read/write error occurs, it prints an error message and skips the sample. The loop continues until the user interrupts the program with Ctrl+C. When the program exits, it closes the I2C handle, closes the file, and terminates the GPIO library.

