This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It initializes the GPIO pin as an input with the internal pull-up resistor enabled, sets up a signal handler to release resources and dump the buffer on receipt of SIGINT, and continuously polls the pin for changes, recording each detection in a circular buffer. When an obstacle is detected, it prints a message to stdout with the timestamp. On receipt of SIGINT, it releases all resources, dumps the buffer to stdout, and exits cleanly.

