This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO chip and lines. It opens the chip, requests the input line for the sensor and the output line for the LED, sets the LED line to low (off), installs SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers, and enters a main loop where it reads the sensor line, turns on the LED if the sensor is touched, and turns off the LED otherwise. The loop sleeps for the poll interval between iterations.

The code logs startup, shutdown, each touch event, and any errors to the system syslog using `openlog` and `syslog`. It also releases all resources when the program exits.

Note that this code assumes that the SainSmart TTP223B digital capacitive touch sensor is connected to GPIO23 (physical pin 16, BCM 23) and the LED is connected to GPIO18 (physical pin 12, BCM 18) with an appropriate current-limiting resistor.

