This code uses the `gpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up two GPIO lines as inputs and two GPIO lines as outputs, and uses a timer to debounce the inputs. When a rising or falling edge is detected on either input, the corresponding LED is turned on or off, and the event is logged to a circular buffer. The log buffer is printed to the console every iteration of the main loop. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to perform a clean shutdown.

