This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a signal handler to catch `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` signals, which will cause the program to exit cleanly by releasing the GPIO line, closing the log file, and terminating the GPIO library.

The main loop continuously checks for a falling edge on the GPIO line, and if one is detected, it prints a message to the console and appends a timestamped message to the log file. The log file is opened in append mode with immediate flush to ensure that the messages are written to the file immediately.

The code also checks for errors on all library calls and file operations, and exits with an error message if any of these operations fail.

