This code uses the `gpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up four GPIO lines as outputs and reads their values every 100ms. The values are then written to a CSV file named `tracking_log.csv`. The code also handles errors and releases resources on exit. The `cleanup` function is called when the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal, which closes the GPIO chip, releases the GPIO lines, and closes the CSV file.

