This code uses the `pigpio` library for GPIO operations and `libgpiod` for I2C operations. It initializes the I2C bus and GPIO, sets up the ADXL345 accelerometer for full-resolution mode with a ±2g range, and reads acceleration data from the device every 100ms. The data is logged to a file named `accel_log.txt` in the format "timestamp,x,y,z" with the three axis values expressed in g units to three decimal places. The program also turns on an active-high LED connected to GPIO17 (BCM numbering) whenever the absolute acceleration on any axis exceeds 2.0g and turns it off otherwise. The program cleanly releases the I2C handle, GPIO, and closes the log file when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

