```

This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the I2C bus. It continuously reads data from the HMC5883L magnetometer, maintains a running average of the last 100 samples to compute hard-iron offsets, applies those offsets to each new raw reading, and prints the offset-corrected X, Y, and Z components to stdout every 500 ms. If an I2C read or write error occurs, it is explicitly flagged on stderr without causing the program to crash. The application cleanly releases the I2C handle and any driver resources when it receives SIGINT or SIGTERM.

