This code uses the `gpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a timer to poll the sound sensor every 100 ms, and when a sound event is detected, it activates the relay for 3 seconds and logs the timestamp to a file. The relay is not retriggered while it is already active due to the debounce mechanism. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to ensure a clean shutdown.

