This code uses the `gpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up the rain sensor as an event-driven input and the motor as an output. When the rain sensor detects a rising edge, it starts the motor and holds it for 5 seconds. The motor is stopped when the rain sensor goes high again. The code also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to perform a clean shutdown.

