This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up the GPIO pins, reads the HX711 amplifier, and logs the weight to the syslog. If the weight exceeds the threshold, it activates the solenoid lock. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to perform a clean shutdown.

