This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up a signal handler for `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` to turn the relay off and release the GPIO resources when the program is interrupted. The `check_sensor` function checks the state of the sensor pin and toggles the relay if a valid rising edge is detected. The `toggle_relay` function updates the relay state and logs the change to the console. The `main` function parses the command-line argument for the debounce interval and initializes the GPIO.

