This code uses the `libgpiod` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It initializes the GPIO pin as an input with an internal pull-up resistor, sets it to trigger on rising edges, and enables a 2ms debounce window to reject contact bounce and double-edge noise. It then enters a loop where it waits for events on the GPIO line, counts the number of pulses, and calculates the RPM every 5 seconds. The RPM is logged to a file and printed to the console. The program exits cleanly when a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal is received.

