This code implements a PID speed control for two L298N-driven DC motors equipped with quadrature encoders using the GPIO bus on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the pigpio library for GPIO access and the pthread library for multithreading. The program reads the encoder counts in separate threads and computes the PID output in the main thread. The PID output is used to set the duty cycle of the PWM signals to the motors. The program logs the motor speeds, P, I, and D components, and the PID output to a file named motor_log.csv. The program runs indefinitely until interrupted by a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

