Please note that this code assumes that the BH1750 light sensor is connected to the I2C bus 1 and the relay is connected to GPIO 23 (BCM). You may need to adjust the I2C bus and GPIO pin numbers to match your specific setup.

This code also assumes that the `grow_log.txt` file is in the same directory as the executable. If you want to log to a different file, you will need to modify the `LOG_FILE` macro accordingly.

Finally, this code uses the `sigaction` system call to set up a signal handler for the `SIGINT` signal. When the program receives a `SIGINT` signal (e.g. when you press `Ctrl+C`), the signal handler will be called, which will close the I2C handle, turn off the relay, and exit the program cleanly.

